<gpx version="1.1" creator="book_route.py" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1">
<metadata><name>Gates of the Mountain</name><desc>or-vielbig-2e:198-4: route read from the book's text and sketch map. One trkseg per waypoint pair, in order; segment sources are in the trk desc. Geometry from OSM (ODbL, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors) and USFS EDW (public domain) where marked; 'straight' segments are off-trail connectors, not traced.</desc></metadata>
<wpt lat="45.321340" lon="-121.617170"><ele>1299.1</ele><name>Clark Creek Sno-Park</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin th:clark-creek-sno-park (on OR 35; lot unmapped); confidence: medium; pdf_page: 197; quote: From Clark Creek Sno-Park ski a trail 150 yards to the junction where the Clark Creek Trail starts. Here turn left</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.324222" lon="-121.620670"><ele>1325.7</ele><name>Old Elk Meadows Trail, east end</name><desc>source: OSM way 146985885 'Old Elk Meadows Trail' east end (the 1.2-mile built-for-skiing trail); confidence: medium; pdf_page: 197; quote: at first along a 1.2-mile built-for-skiing trail to the Clark Creek single-log bridge</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.328930" lon="-121.630932"><ele>1387.7</ele><name>Joins the summer Elk Meadows Trail (Clark Creek bridge)</name><desc>source: OSM: Old Elk Meadows Trail meets Elk Meadows Trail #645; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 197; quote: to the Clark Creek single-log bridge where it joins the summer Elk Meadows hiking trail</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.334935" lon="-121.626145"><ele>1405.3</ele><name>Newton Creek crossing</name><desc>source: OSM node 1601784626, end of Newton Creek Trail #646 on #645; DEM 4,610 ft; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 201; book_elev_ft: 4640; quote: Ski the Elk Meadows Trail to Newton Creek. Do not cross the creek but enter the forest</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.336019" lon="-121.628664"><ele>1426.5</ele><name>Forest on the south-west bank 1</name><desc>source: placed 130-150 m SW of OSM Newton Creek (way 150578135) on the gentle bench beside it (DEM cross-sections); confidence: low; pdf_page: 201; quote: enter the forest and parallel the creek on gentle grades for about 0.5 mile</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.337638" lon="-121.631824"><ele>1445.6</ele><name>Forest on the south-west bank 2</name><desc>source: placed 130-150 m SW of OSM Newton Creek (way 150578135) on the gentle bench beside it (DEM cross-sections); confidence: low; pdf_page: 201; quote: enter the forest and parallel the creek on gentle grades for about 0.5 mile</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.339318" lon="-121.632446"><ele>1459.3</ele><name>Forest on the south-west bank 3</name><desc>source: placed 130-150 m SW of OSM Newton Creek (way 150578135) on the gentle bench beside it (DEM cross-sections); confidence: low; pdf_page: 201; quote: enter the forest and parallel the creek on gentle grades for about 0.5 mile</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.341830" lon="-121.634390"><ele>1483.6</ele><name>Down into the creek bed, where it becomes skiable</name><desc>source: node of OSM Newton Creek (way 150578135); confidence: low; pdf_page: 201; quote: As you get higher the creek bottom becomes skiable</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.344100" lon="-121.636180"><ele>1505.8</ele><name>Newton Creek bed 1</name><desc>source: node of OSM Newton Creek (way 150578135); confidence: medium; pdf_page: 201; quote: it is followed on a twisting course upward into the great, wide valley below the cliffs of Gnarl Ridge and Lamberson Butte</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.346110" lon="-121.636330"><ele>1524.7</ele><name>Newton Creek bed 2</name><desc>source: node of OSM Newton Creek (way 150578135); confidence: medium; pdf_page: 201; quote: it is followed on a twisting course upward into the great, wide valley below the cliffs of Gnarl Ridge and Lamberson Butte</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="45.348330" lon="-121.639700"><ele>1555.7</ele><name>Newton Creek bed 3</name><desc>source: node of OSM Newton Creek (way 150578135); confidence: medium; pdf_page: 201; quote: it is followed on a twisting course upward into the great, wide valley below the cliffs of Gnarl Ridge and Lamberson Butte</desc></wpt>
